      "text": "First, identify the pattern of the sequence. We see that the sequence is a geometric sequence where each term is twice the previous term. The sequence is: \\(1, 2, 4, 8, 16, \\ldots, 1024\\).\n\nThis sequence can be written as: \\(1, 2, 4, 8, 16, \\ldots, 1024\\).\n\nTo find the sum, we recognize that this is a geometric series where the first term \\(a = 1\\) and the common ratio \\(r = 2\\).\n\nThe sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of a geometric series is given by:\n\\[\nS_n = a \\frac{r^n - 1}{r - 1}\n\\]\n\nHere, the number of terms \\(n\\) can be determined by noting that the \\(n\\)-th term of the sequence is \\(2^{n-1}\\), and we need the \\(n\\)-th term to be 1024:\n\\[\n2^{n-1} = 1024\n\\]\n\nSince \\(1024 = 2^{10}\\), we have:\n\\[\n2^{n-1} = 2^{10} \\implies n-1 = 10 \\implies n = 11\n\\]\n\nSo, there are 11 terms in the sequence. Now, we substitute \\(a = 1\\), \\(r = 2\\), and \\(n = 11\\) into the sum formula:\n\\[\nS_{11} = 1 \\frac{2^{11} - 1}{2 - 1} = 2^{11} - 1\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(2^{11}\\):\n\\[\n2^{11} = 2048\n\\]\n\nThus, the sum \\(S_{11}\\) is:\n\\[\nS_{11} = 2048 - 1 = 2047\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the sequence \\(1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + \\cdots + 1024\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2047}\n\\]",
