      "text": "To find the sum of the geometric series \\(1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + \\cdots + 1024\\), we first need to understand the structure of the series. This is a geometric series with the first term \\(a = 1\\) and the common ratio \\(r = 2\\).\n\nThe general form of the \\(n\\)-th term of a geometric series is given by:\n\\[a_n = a \\cdot r^{n-1}\\]\n\nIn this series, the \\(n\\)-th term is \\(1 \\cdot 2^{n-1} = 2^{n-1}\\). We need to find the number of terms in the series. The last term is \\(1024\\), which is \\(2^{10}\\). Therefore, the series has 11 terms (from \\(2^0\\) to \\(2^{10}\\)).\n\nThe sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of a geometric series is given by:\n\\[S_n = a \\frac{r^n - 1}{r - 1}\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(a = 1\\), \\(r = 2\\), and \\(n = 11\\), we get:\n\\[S_{11} = 1 \\cdot \\frac{2^{11} - 1}{2 - 1} = 2^{11} - 1\\]\n\nNow, we calculate \\(2^{11}\\):\n\\[2^{11} = 2048\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum is:\n\\[S_{11} = 2048 - 1 = 2047\\]\n\nSo, the sum of the series \\(1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + \\cdots + 1024\\) is \\(\\boxed{2047}\\).",
