      "text": "To determine the sum of the given series \\(1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + \\cdots + 1024\\), we first recognize that this is a geometric series. A geometric series is a series with a constant ratio between successive terms. Here, the first term \\(a\\) is 1 and the common ratio \\(r\\) is 2.\n\nThe general form of the \\(n\\)-th term of a geometric series is given by:\n\\[a_n = a \\cdot r^{n-1}\\]\n\nFor our series, the \\(n\\)-th term is:\n\\[a_n = 2^{n-1}\\]\n\nThe series given is:\n\\[1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + \\cdots + 1024\\]\n\nWe need to find the number of terms \\(n\\) in this series. The last term is 1024, so we set up the equation:\n\\[2^{n-1} = 1024\\]\n\nWe know that:\n\\[1024 = 2^{10}\\]\n\nThus, we have:\n\\[2^{n-1} = 2^{10}\\]\n\nBy equating the exponents, we get:\n\\[n-1 = 10\\]\n\\[n = 11\\]\n\nSo, the series has 11 terms. The sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of a geometric series is given by:\n\\[S_n = a \\frac{r^n - 1}{r - 1}\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(a = 1\\), \\(r = 2\\), and \\(n = 11\\), we get:\n\\[S_{11} = 1 \\frac{2^{11} - 1}{2 - 1} = 2^{11} - 1\\]\n\nCalculating \\(2^{11}\\):\n\\[2^{11} = 2048\\]\n\nThus:\n\\[S_{11} = 2048 - 1 = 2047\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series \\(1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + \\cdots + 1024\\) is:\n\\[\\boxed{2047}\\]",
